You have normal tension glaucoma in one or both eyes. This is a form of glaucoma in which the optic nerve is damaged even though the measured eye pressure is within the usual population range.\
\
This happens because some optic nerves are more vulnerable to pressure-related stress or to reduced blood flow than others. As with other forms of glaucoma, side vision is usually affected first, and changes often occur without obvious symptoms.\
